    prompt: `Write a performance review self-assessment covering:\n\nSection 1 — Key Achievements (most important section):\n- List 5-8 specific accomplishments with measurable impact\n- Use the format: "Accomplished [X] as measured by [Y] by doing [Z]"\n- Include: revenue impact, time saved, quality improved, team helped, customers delighted\n- For each: what was the situation, what did YOU specifically do, what was the result\n\nSection 2 — Goals Review:\n- List last period's goals and rate each: Exceeded / Met / Partially Met / Not Met\n- For "Partially Met": explain blockers honestly and what you learned\n- For "Not Met": own it, explain why, and what you'd do differently\n\nSection 3 — Strengths Demonstrated:\n- 3-5 strengths with specific examples\n- Technical strengths (languages, systems, architecture)\n- Soft skills (leadership, communication, mentoring, cross-team collaboration)\n- Connect each to business value created\n\nSection 4 — Growth & Development:\n- Skills you developed this period\n- Courses, books, conferences, or certifications completed\n- New responsibilities you took on\n- Feedback you received and how you acted on it\n\nSection 5 — Areas for Improvement:\n- 2-3 honest areas where you want to grow\n- Specific plan for each (course, mentorship, stretch project)\n- Frame positively: "I want to develop deeper expertise in..." not "I'm bad at..."\n\nSection 6 — Goals for Next Period:\n- 3-5 SMART goals aligned with team/company OKRs\n- Include both delivery goals and growth goals\n- Specific, measurable targets with deadlines\n\nSection 7 — Feedback for Manager/Company:\n- What support do you need to succeed?\n- What processes could improve?\n- Career aspirations (promotion path, role change, new challenges)\n\nTone: Confident and factual, not arrogant. Own your wins. Be honest about growth areas. Show self-awareness.`,
