    category: "design-ux",
    icon: "&#x1F4D0;",
    title: "Responsive Grid Framework",
    description: "Build a responsive layout grid system with breakpoints, container queries, and compositional patterns.",
    prompt: `Build a responsive layout grid framework:\n\nBreakpoint System:\n- Mobile-first approach (min-width breakpoints)\n- xs: 0px (default, no media query)\n- sm: 640px (large phones)\n- md: 768px (tablets)\n- lg: 1024px (small laptops)\n- xl: 1280px (desktops)\n- 2xl: 1536px (large screens)\n\nContainer:\n- max-width per breakpoint: sm=640px, md=768px, lg=1024px, xl=1280px\n- Centered with auto margins\n- Padding: 1rem on mobile, 1.5rem on tablet, 2rem on desktop\n\nGrid System (CSS Grid):\n- 12-column grid\n- Gap scale: 0.5rem, 1rem, 1.5rem, 2rem, 3rem\n- Column span utilities: .col-1 through .col-12\n- Responsive column spans: .col-sm-6, .col-md-4, .col-lg-3\n- Auto-fit/auto-fill grid for card layouts: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(300px, 1fr))\n- Nested grids support\n\nLayout Patterns (pre-built):\n- Sidebar + Content: sidebar 250-300px fixed, content fluid\n- Holy Grail: header, footer, left sidebar, content, right sidebar\n- Card grid: 2-4 columns responsive with equal height cards\n- Dashboard: grid-template-areas for complex widget layouts\n- Split screen: 50/50 columns with optional reversed stacking\n\nContainer Queries (modern alternative to media queries):\n- Define containers with container-type: inline-size\n- Query syntax: @container (min-width: 400px) { ... }\n- Use for components that appear in different contexts (narrow sidebar vs. wide main content)\n- Fallback strategy for browsers without container query support\n\nSpacing System:\n- Padding and margin utility classes based on the scale\n- Responsive spacing: .p-4 .p-md-6 .p-lg-8\n- Section spacing: larger vertical rhythm between page sections\n\nAlignment Utilities:\n- Flexbox: justify-content, align-items, flex-direction, gap\n- Grid: place-items, place-content\n- Self-alignment: justify-self, align-self\n\nCSS Implementation:\n- Custom properties for breakpoints, container widths, and grid gaps\n- Utility-first CSS classes (similar to Tailwind but custom)\n- No JavaScript dependency\n- IE11 not supported\n\nProvide the complete CSS and a demo page with all layout patterns rendered.`,
