    prompt: `Create an API integration guide for [API Name / Service]:\n\nQuick start:\n- Prerequisites (accounts, keys, versions)\n- Install SDK or HTTP client\n- Authentication setup (API key, OAuth, JWT)\n- Make your first API call (3-5 lines of code)\n- Verify it worked (expected response)\n\nAuthentication deep-dive:\n- How to obtain credentials\n- Token format and expiration\n- Refresh flow (if applicable)\n- Security best practices:\n  - Store keys in environment variables, never commit\n  - Use server-side calls when possible (protect secrets)\n  - Rotate keys regularly\n\nCore endpoints with examples:\nFor each major endpoint category:\n- HTTP method and URL\n- Request parameters (path, query, body) with types\n- Example request (curl + code in 2 languages)\n- Example response with explanation of key fields\n- Common error responses and how to handle them\n\nPagination:\n- Pagination method (offset, cursor, page)\n- How to iterate through all results\n- Rate limits and how to handle (retry-after, exponential backoff)\n\nWebhooks:\n- How to subscribe to events\n- Webhook payload format\n- How to verify webhook signatures (security)\n- Recommended response (200 OK immediately, process async)\n\nError handling:\n- HTTP status codes and what they mean\n- Retry strategy per error type\n- Logging: what to log, what not to log (PII, secrets)\n- Circuit breaker pattern for dependent services\n\nBest practices:\n- Use idempotency keys for POST/PUT to prevent duplicates\n- Batch requests when possible (reduce round trips)\n- Implement request timeout (don't hang indefinitely)\n- Validate responses against expected schema\n- Handle API versioning (version header or URL path)\n\nTesting:\n- Sandbox/test environment setup\n- Mock API responses for unit tests\n- Integration test with sandbox\n\nSDK generation:\n- Generate types from OpenAPI/Swagger spec (openapi-generator, quicktype)\n- Type-safe API client wrapper\n\nProvide code examples in JavaScript/TypeScript and Python. Include Postman collection export.`,
