    description: "Create a comprehensive contributor's guide to attract and onboard open source contributors effectively.",
    prompt: `Create an open source contribution guide:\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md structure:\n\nWelcome section (be human):\n- Thank potential contributors for their interest\n- Brief project mission (1-2 sentences)\n- Types of contributions needed (code, docs, design, testing, community)\n- Link to Code of Conduct\n\nGetting started (make it stupidly easy):\n- Prerequisites (Node.js version, Python version, Docker, etc.)\n- Clone and setup (copy-paste commands):\n  git clone ...\n  cd project\n  npm install\n  cp .env.example .env\n  npm run dev\n- Verify setup: open localhost:3000, you should see...\n- Common setup issues and solutions\n\nProject structure overview:\n- Top-level directory map with brief descriptions\n- Architecture decisions (ADR links or brief explanations of why things are the way they are)\n- Key files to understand first\n\nDevelopment workflow:\n- Branch naming convention (feature/, fix/, docs/)\n- Commit message convention (Conventional Commits or similar)\n- How to run tests\n- How to run linters/formatters\n- Pre-commit hooks setup\n\nHow to find something to work on:\n- Good First Issue label (with estimated effort and mentor)\n- Help Wanted label\n- Issue triage: how we prioritize\n- If no suitable issue exists, how to propose one\n\nMaking a Pull Request:\n- Fork the repo\n- Create a branch\n- Make changes (with tests!)\n- Run tests and linters\n- Push and open PR\n- Fill out PR template (link issue, describe changes, add screenshots)\n- What happens after you open a PR:\n  - CI runs automatically\n  - A maintainer will review within X days\n  - You may get feedback and need to make changes\n  - Once approved, a maintainer will merge\n\nCode style guide:\n- Link to style guide or inline key rules\n- Naming conventions\n- Comment policy (when to comment, when not to)\n- Testing expectations (at least 1 test per new feature/fix)\n- Documentation expectations (update docs with code changes)\n\nCommunity:\n- Discord/Slack community link\n- Office hours or pair programming sessions\n- How to become a maintainer\n\nRecognition:\n- All contributors list (link or automated)\n- Contributor spotlight (blog, tweet, etc.)\n- Swag program (stickers, t-shirts for significant contributions)\n\nLicense:\n- Brief note about license\n- Link to full LICENSE file\n\nISSUE_TEMPLATE and PR_TEMPLATE:\n- Bug report template: version, steps to reproduce, expected vs. actual, screenshots\n- Feature request template: problem, proposed solution, alternatives considered\n- PR template: what, why, how to test, screenshots, checklist\n\nKeep the tone welcoming, inclusive, and patient. Assume good intent. Use "we" language. Show appreciation.`,
