    prompt: `Build a production WebSocket server for [use case, e.g., chat, live collaboration, gaming]:\n\nCore Server (Node.js with ws or Socket.io):\n- Connection lifecycle: onConnect → authenticate → join rooms → onDisconnect\n- Authentication: validate JWT token on connection upgrade\n- Heartbeat: ping/pong every 30s, disconnect after 90s of silence\n- Reconnection: client reconnects with session token, rejoins rooms\n\nRoom Management:\n- createRoom(roomId, options) — with max capacity, password, persistence\n- joinRoom(socket, roomId) — validate permissions, notify room members\n- leaveRoom(socket, roomId) — cleanup, notify\n- Room metadata: name, member count, topic, created at\n- List rooms: with filtering (public vs private, by tag)\n\nPresence System:\n- Track online users per room\n- Broadcast join/leave events to room\n- User status: online, idle (no activity for 5min), offline\n- Custom presence data: typing indicator, cursor position, current view\n- Get room presence: list all online users with their status\n\nEvent Broadcasting:\n- to(roomId).emit(event, data) — send to all in room\n- to(roomId).except(socketId).emit(event, data)\n- to(socketId).emit(event, data) — send to specific user\n- Event schema validation with zod at the server level\n- Event types: system (join, leave, error), custom (message, update, cursor)\n\nPersistence Layer:\n- Message history: store in PostgreSQL, load on room join (last 50 messages)\n- Room state: persist to Redis for fast recovery on server restart\n- Session store: Redis with TTL for reconnection tokens\n\nHorizontal Scaling:\n- Redis Pub/Sub adapter for multi-process communication\n- Consistent hashing for room-to-server assignment\n- Graceful shutdown: drain connections, transfer rooms to other servers\n- Sticky sessions via load balancer (nginx ip_hash or HAProxy)\n\nRate Limiting & Security:\n- Per-socket message rate limit (10 msg/sec, burst 20)\n- Per-room creation limit (max 100 per server)\n- Max connections per IP\n- Input sanitization: strip HTML, enforce max message length\n- CORS: only allow configured origins\n\nMonitoring:\n- Active connections gauge\n- Messages per second counter\n- Room count gauge\n- Connection duration histogram\n- Error rate by event type\n\nClient SDK:\n- WebSocket wrapper with auto-reconnect, message queue, event typing\n- React hook: useSocket(url, options) → { send, lastMessage, readyState }\n- TypeScript types generated from event schema\n\nProvide complete server implementation, Redis adapter, and a basic React chat UI client.`,
