    title: "Payment Integration Guide",
    description: "Integrate Stripe or equivalent payment processing with checkout flow, webhooks, and subscription management.",
    prompt: `Integrate payment processing using [Stripe/Paddle/LemonSqueezy]:\n\nOne-Time Payment Flow:\n- Client: create payment intent → confirm with Stripe Elements or Checkout\n- Server: create Checkout Session with line items, success/cancel URLs\n- Webhook: payment_intent.succeeded → fulfill order, send receipt\n- Error handling: card declined, insufficient funds, expired card\n\nSubscription Flow:\n- Define Products and Prices in Stripe Dashboard (or via API)\n- Client: redirect to Checkout with subscription mode\n- Server webhook: checkout.session.completed → provision access\n- Recurring: invoice.paid → extend subscription, invoice.payment_failed → notify user\n- Cancel: update subscription status, schedule cancellation at period end\n- Reactivate: allow reactivation within grace period\n\nCustomer Portal:\n- Stripe Customer Portal for self-service: update payment method, view invoices, cancel\n- Custom billing page if more control needed (list subscriptions, change plan, download invoices)\n\nWebhook Handling:\n- Verify webhook signature (critical — prevents spoofed events)\n- Idempotency: use idempotency key, check if event already processed\n- Retry: queue webhook processing, retry on failure\n- Log all webhook events for debugging\n- Monitor: webhook success rate, processing latency\n\nSecurity:\n- NEVER handle raw card numbers (use Stripe Elements or Checkout)\n- PCI compliance: Stripe.js handles sensitive data, your server never sees card numbers\n- Idempotency keys for all mutation operations\n- Rate limit checkout and subscription endpoints\n\nTesting:\n- Stripe test mode: use test card numbers (4242 4242 4242 4242)\n- Test all webhook events locally with Stripe CLI\n- Test: successful payment, failed payment, 3D Secure, disputes, refunds\n- Test subscription lifecycle: trial → active → past_due → canceled → unpaid\n\nDatabase Schema:\n- subscriptions: id, user_id, stripe_subscription_id, plan_id, status, current_period_end\n- customers: id, user_id, stripe_customer_id\n- invoices: id, subscription_id, stripe_invoice_id, amount, status, paid_at\n\nProvide the complete integration with server and client code.`,
