    id: "career-14",
    category: "career-resume",
    icon: "&#x1F3AF;",
    title: "Personal Brand Building Plan",
    description: "Create a 6-month personal brand strategy with content, speaking, and community engagement.",
    prompt: `Create a 6-month personal brand building plan for [your name/role]:\n\nDefine Your Brand:\n- Your niche: [specific intersection of skills, e.g., "frontend performance for e-commerce"]\n- Your unique perspective: what do you believe that others don't? (controversial but defensible)\n- Your audience: who are you writing/speaking for? (junior devs, engineering managers, founders)\n- Your content pillars (3-4): topics you'll consistently cover\n- Your voice: [e.g., practical and no-nonsense, thoughtful and philosophical, funny and relatable]\n\nMonth 1 — Foundation:\n- Audit existing online presence (LinkedIn, Twitter/X, GitHub, personal site)\n- Optimize LinkedIn profile (see LinkedIn optimization prompt for details)\n- Create/polish personal website with: about, blog, projects, speaking, contact\n- Define content calendar: post at least 2x per week on [primary platform]\n- Start a newsletter or blog (choose one platform, be consistent)\n\nMonth 2 — Content Engine:\n- Publish 4 blog posts/newsletters (one per week)\n- Share each post across platforms with platform-native formatting\n- Engage daily: comment on 10 posts in your niche (add value, not "great post!")\n- Join 2-3 communities (Discord, Slack, Reddit) and participate regularly\n- Reach out to 5 people for virtual coffee chats\n\nMonth 3 — Amplification:\n- Guest post on 2 industry blogs or publications\n- Appear on 1-2 podcasts (pitch yourself to hosts: what unique perspective can you offer?)\n- Create 1 piece of original research or a data-driven post (highest shareability)\n- Start building an email list (lead magnet: free guide, template, or tool)\n\nMonth 4 — Speaking & Visibility:\n- Submit talks to 3 CFPs (Call for Proposals) for meetups or conferences\n- Give a talk at a local meetup or company event\n- Create video content: 1 tutorial or talk recording per month\n- Collaborate: co-author a post or co-host a webinar with someone in your network\n\nMonth 5 — Deepen Expertise:\n- Launch a side project or open source contribution (something tangible to point to)\n- Write a comprehensive guide on your niche topic (the definitive resource)\n- Mentor 2-3 junior people in your field (builds reputation and network)\n- Attend 1 conference (virtual or in-person), meet 10 new people\n\nMonth 6 — Evaluate and Pivot:\n- Review metrics: followers, newsletter subscribers, website traffic, inbound opportunities\n- What content performed best? Double down on that format and topic\n- What didn't work? Cut it\n- Plan next 6 months based on data\n\nContent Ideas Bank (30+ topics ready to write about):\n- Lessons learned from [project/failure]\n- How to [achieve specific outcome] in [timeframe]\n- Comparison: [Tool A] vs [Tool B] — when to use which\n- My [morning routine / dev setup / productivity system]\n- The biggest misconception about [your niche]\n- A contrarian take on [industry trend]\n- Behind the scenes of [project]\n- What I wish I knew when I started in [field]\n- Book/podcast recommendations with key takeaways\n- Predictions for [industry] in [next year]\n\nMetrics to Track:\n- Newsletter: subscribers, open rate, click rate\n- LinkedIn: profile views, connection requests, post impressions/engagement\n- Twitter/X: followers, tweet impressions, engagement rate\n- Blog: page views, time on page, inbound links\n- Inbound: speaking invitations, podcast invitations, job offers, client inquiries\n\nProvide the complete 26-week calendar with specific content ideas for each week.`,
    tags: ["personal-brand", "career", "content", "speaking"]
